#
# READING (the pre-registered "spill -> ~0, peak <=32" gate -> ★REACHED / HOLDS):
#   spill  619 -> 7 (-O2) / 603 -> 7 (-O3)  : the S6 stack-panel DROVE spill to ~0 (a −98.9% collapse). The
#                          q2_K untiled full-unroll body carried ~600 whole-register spills — NOT the q4_K
#                          golden 84, but a q6_K-magnitude ~600 — YET, unlike q6_K, that pressure is EXACTLY the
#                          decode-4bit-scale/min strips + the idle-across-the-hot-dot i32 MIN (bsums) accumulator
#                          that the S6 int16/i32 panels stage. So staging them collapses the whole spill set.
#   maxVreg v31 -> v30 (both -O2/-O3) : the peak live-set DROPPED to v30 (<=32 register cliff REACHED — same
#                          v31->v30 step q4_K S6 hit). q6_K never left v31; q2_K does.
#   vwmacc 2304 -> 2304 (UNCHANGED across ALL four) => the widening-MAC multiset is PRESERVED => byte-exact-
#                          preserving schedule (independently confirmed: silicon verify INT_mismatch=0 for BOTH +
#                          the untiled-vs-tiled IDENTITY cmp, 0 mismatch on 32768/8192 floats).
#   textB 51014 -> 26968 (-O2)  : the tiled body is HALF the code — the fully-unrolled spill-and-reload sequence
#                          collapses into a compact panel store/load + a hot dot that fits registers.
#   vsetvli 77 -> 87 : the tiled adds a few vtype toggles for the panel vse16/vle16 + vse32/vle32 store/load bands
#                          (idle-strip staging), but the hot dot itself is register-resident.
#
# ★ CONTRAST WITH q6_K T3 (cell l1-t3-q6k-repack-gemm): there the SAME lever was a NULL — spill 913->949 (UP),
#   maxVreg v31->v31 (cliff NOT reached), throughput −1.5% — because q6_K's ~900-spill pressure lives in the
#   DUAL-PLANE 6-bit weight reconstruction (ql@1312 + qh@288), which the decode-scale panel does not touch.
#   q2_K's ~600-spill pressure lives in the SCALE/MIN decode + MIN accumulator — EXACTLY the panel's target —
#   so here it collapses to ~0. This is the tiling-lever transfer BOUNDARY (C3′ pattern-library): the q4_K S6
#   register-cliff lever transfers to formats whose peak pressure IS the decode/min strips (q4_K/q5_K/q2_K —
#   the shared kquant_dmin_bsums_min fold), and is a null where the peak pressure is dual-plane weight
#   materialization (q6_K). q2_K CONFIRMS the register-cliff prediction; q6_K refuted it.
#
# hot-loop spill classification (TILED -O2, objdump -d — only 7 vs*r.v TOTAL, so all shown):
#   the residual 7 vs*r.v are NOT in the hot dot body — 5 cluster in the prologue (0xd2/0xe6/0x10e/0x20a/0x21a)
#   and 2 at the far epilogue (0x35d8/0x35e8). These are benign function-boundary whole-register saves, the same
#   pattern as q4_K S6's benign residual-3 — NOT hot-loop allocator live-value spills.
